"Fishing Hole"

23
00:01:42,090 --> 00:01:43,220
"Fishing Hole"

24
00:01:42,090 --> 00:01:43,220
Hey! The thing you asked
your friend for came!

25
00:01:43,220 --> 00:01:47,120
Hey! The thing you asked
your friend for came!

26
00:01:52,260 --> 00:01:56,270
Oh that. You brought it for me.

27
00:01:56,270 --> 00:01:57,440
Yeah...

28
00:01:57,440 --> 00:02:01,270
I wanted to see the joy in your face.

29
00:02:01,270 --> 00:02:02,540
Hmm...

30
00:02:05,440 --> 00:02:07,170
This is great.

31
00:02:19,650 --> 00:02:21,810
You're Maho-chan, right?

32
00:02:23,680 --> 00:02:24,740
Huh?

33
00:02:29,820 --> 00:02:32,690
And you were...Izumi-chan?

34
00:02:35,160 --> 00:02:38,000
And it says, "I love New York."

35
00:02:38,000 --> 00:02:41,270
And I got to touch him
when he was running away.

36
00:02:41,270 --> 00:02:43,940
Huh? You touched him?

37
00:02:43,940 --> 00:02:45,130
Neat!

38
00:02:51,450 --> 00:02:53,210
I wanted to talk to you.

39
00:02:58,620 --> 00:03:00,790
Do you have some time now?

40
00:03:00,790 --> 00:03:01,960
Nope.

41
00:03:01,960 --> 00:03:03,790
Oh...

42
00:03:03,790 --> 00:03:06,490
Hmm...Ten minutes is all I need.

43
00:03:08,130 --> 00:03:10,650
Tea? My treat.

44
00:03:26,480 --> 00:03:31,490
I don't know what happened
between you and Maho.

45
00:03:31,490 --> 00:03:32,920
And I don't care.

46
00:03:36,160 --> 00:03:37,920
But...

47
00:03:37,920 --> 00:03:40,090
Hey Koyuki...

48
00:03:40,090 --> 00:03:44,620
The stronger a person looks,
the weaker he is.

49
00:03:48,940 --> 00:03:52,410
Maho looks strong,

50
00:03:52,410 --> 00:03:54,770
but at home, she cries all the time.

51
00:04:12,790 --> 00:04:16,960
Anyway, I have no right to lecture you.

52
00:04:26,310 --> 00:04:27,770
Go!

53
00:04:31,140 --> 00:04:36,170
So what...how do you feel
about my kid sister?

54
00:05:25,970 --> 00:05:27,130
Huh?

55
00:05:27,130 --> 00:05:29,300
Where's Koyuki?

56
00:05:29,300 --> 00:05:32,070
Huh? He went to look for Maho.

57
00:05:32,070 --> 00:05:32,970
Huh?

58
00:05:32,970 --> 00:05:36,840
Maho went to return a video
and hasn't returned for three hours.

59
00:05:38,950 --> 00:05:41,310
Maho?

60
00:05:41,310 --> 00:05:44,820
Don't tell me he's gonna miss
this important meeting for a date!

61
00:05:44,820 --> 00:05:47,590
-Huh? Date?
-That Koyuki!

62
00:05:47,590 --> 00:05:49,590
Here...I brought something.

63
00:05:49,590 --> 00:05:50,820
Thanks.

64
00:06:29,660 --> 00:06:34,170
"Neighborhood Watch-
Work together to prevent crime"

65
00:06:34,170 --> 00:06:39,230
"Liquor, Cigarettes"
"Exciting Town"

66
00:06:46,780 --> 00:06:48,080
Uh?

67
00:06:48,080 --> 00:06:49,280
Huh?

68
00:07:28,290 --> 00:07:30,790
See you, Koyuki.

69
00:07:30,790 --> 00:07:34,160
Huh? Izumi-chan...

70
00:07:36,130 --> 00:07:38,360
Good-bye, Koyuki.

71
00:08:11,430 --> 00:08:13,660
Good-bye, Koyuki.

72
00:08:19,940 --> 00:08:22,940
I don't understand Japanese thinking.

73
00:08:22,940 --> 00:08:24,280
Huh?

74
00:08:24,280 --> 00:08:28,110
She hunted me down just to tell me...

75
00:08:28,110 --> 00:08:32,210
that there's nothing between you and her.

76
00:08:35,960 --> 00:08:41,120
At first I thought,
"What the hell do you want?"

77
00:08:42,730 --> 00:08:46,400
After talking to her...
man, she's really nice.

78
00:08:46,400 --> 00:08:51,030
But she seems more like your older sister.

79
00:08:58,080 --> 00:08:59,910
Want to go eat a burger?

80
00:08:59,910 --> 00:09:03,080
Err...no. Ryusuke was worried.

81
00:09:03,080 --> 00:09:04,140
No shit?

82
00:09:05,250 --> 00:09:09,020
But he never acts like a big brother...

83
00:09:14,590 --> 00:09:16,930
Not that article again?

84
00:09:16,930 --> 00:09:18,960
Why're you so stuck on it?

85
00:09:21,270 --> 00:09:24,900
At one time, Eddy and Erica used to date.

86
00:09:28,440 --> 00:09:33,110
We had gone to the
Appollon Theater Amateur Night

87
00:09:33,110 --> 00:09:35,880
and saw Erica before she debuted.

88
00:09:38,220 --> 00:09:42,220
Her powerful singing voice blew me away.

89
00:09:42,220 --> 00:09:48,060
That was the one and only time
we ever waited for someone backstage.

90
00:09:48,060 --> 00:09:53,570
But Eddy and Erica couldn't
get past their problems.

91
00:09:53,570 --> 00:09:55,430
Their relationship didn't last long.

92
00:09:57,970 --> 00:10:01,070
To think that someone
who had such strong vibes

93
00:10:01,070 --> 00:10:05,070
would commit suicide like that...
I just can't believe it.

94
00:10:07,080 --> 00:10:08,180
Hmm...

95
00:10:08,180 --> 00:10:10,080
You think it was murder?

96
00:10:10,080 --> 00:10:12,640
Even the FBI is suspicious.

97
00:10:15,090 --> 00:10:17,890
And the one who benefited most
from Erica's death...

98
00:10:19,990 --> 00:10:21,520
Hmm...

99
00:10:22,600 --> 00:10:25,560
The rapper boyfriend...Malcolm.

100
00:10:29,440 --> 00:10:32,430
Yes. Thank you.

101
00:10:37,710 --> 00:10:39,710
Man, it's totally over.

102
00:10:39,710 --> 00:10:41,710
Hey, are you serious?!

103
00:10:41,710 --> 00:10:44,050
Then that offer from major label...

104
00:10:44,050 --> 00:10:47,490
Just means life ain't so easy.

105
00:10:49,660 --> 00:10:55,560
Wait! I know! Your letters
made the record company mad!

106
00:10:55,560 --> 00:10:56,230
Huh?

107
00:10:56,230 --> 00:11:02,740
Well look...During Dying Breed's
live performance, everything seemed fine!

108
00:11:02,740 --> 00:11:07,410
Well probably...Ran's power
is greater than we thought.

109
00:11:07,410 --> 00:11:08,410
Him?

110
00:11:08,410 --> 00:11:11,580
I get it. So that's how it is.

111
00:11:11,580 --> 00:11:16,420
On top of losing the debut
for Belle Ame, he became a back-up.

112
00:11:16,420 --> 00:11:19,320
He must be mad as hell.

113
00:11:24,420 --> 00:11:28,430
We got ourselves some enemy.

114
00:11:28,430 --> 00:11:31,990
Nah...We just didn't have it.

115
00:11:40,110 --> 00:11:44,280
Excuse me for having
a bad English accent!!

116
00:11:44,280 --> 00:11:46,880
You just don't progress!

117
00:11:46,880 --> 00:11:49,080
And you have a habit of mouthing off!

118
00:11:50,680 --> 00:11:55,620
-I think adding so many
notes about pronunciation...
-Don't lecture me!

119
00:11:55,620 --> 00:11:59,790
Hey Ryusuke...We've been practicing
so much, our motivation is down.

120
00:11:59,790 --> 00:12:02,960
When are we going to record?

121
00:12:02,960 --> 00:12:05,470
-Huh? Record?!
-Huh? Record?!

122
00:12:05,470 --> 00:12:10,160
We have to record the ultimate album,
one the industry won't be able to ignore.

123
00:12:15,480 --> 00:12:21,180
If we sit on our asses,
we'll never reach our dream!

124
00:12:35,330 --> 00:12:36,760
What?

125
00:12:36,760 --> 00:12:40,930
An all-night practice at
the studio again on Saturday night?!

126
00:12:40,930 --> 00:12:41,940
-Uh-huh.
-Uh-huh.

127
00:12:41,940 --> 00:12:44,100
You guys are in such a rush.

128
00:12:44,100 --> 00:12:46,940
Think so? It's been the norm lately.

129
00:12:46,940 --> 00:12:48,780
-Right?
-Yeah.

130
00:12:48,780 --> 00:12:51,950
Hmm...You're really working hard, huh?

131
00:12:51,950 --> 00:12:53,110
Huh?

132
00:12:53,110 --> 00:12:57,050
But hey, when you're famous,
I want your autographs.

133
00:13:09,130 --> 00:13:12,300
"Really working hard" huh?

134
00:13:12,300 --> 00:13:13,970
Isn't that him?

135
00:13:13,970 --> 00:13:17,140
Yeah! He was great
at the Culture Festival.

136
00:13:17,140 --> 00:13:19,640
I heard he performs at various live houses.

137
00:13:19,640 --> 00:13:20,330
Huh?

138
00:13:24,140 --> 00:13:25,580
Hey Tanaka!

139
00:13:29,320 --> 00:13:31,780
Come to my office.

140
00:13:31,780 --> 00:13:33,150
"Teachers' Office"

141
00:13:33,150 --> 00:13:34,250
"Teachers' Office"

142
00:13:33,150 --> 00:13:34,250
Huh!? That much?

143
00:13:34,250 --> 00:13:35,820
Huh!? That much?

144
00:13:35,820 --> 00:13:37,090
Is it a shock?

145
00:13:37,090 --> 00:13:40,560
But that's the reality for you right now.

146
00:13:40,560 --> 00:13:41,590
Oh...

147
00:13:41,590 --> 00:13:43,430
Tachi High is impossible.

148
00:13:43,430 --> 00:13:48,100
Toyonaga West is also a far reach.

149
00:13:48,100 --> 00:13:49,540
Err...I see.

150
00:13:49,540 --> 00:13:51,440
I'll get right to the point.

151
00:13:51,440 --> 00:13:54,460
You need to change your focus.

152
00:13:55,940 --> 00:13:59,280
You were once in the high middle ranking.

153
00:13:59,280 --> 00:14:01,340
Recently, you've plunged.

154
00:14:03,950 --> 00:14:07,450
Tanaka, it's fine to enjoy your youth.

155
00:14:07,450 --> 00:14:11,820
But the rest of your life is on the line.

156
00:14:56,440 --> 00:15:00,770
Yukio! It's late! Turn down the volume.

157
00:15:00,770 --> 00:15:02,170
All right.

158
00:15:09,280 --> 00:15:12,790
Koyuki-kun! Just like this-108 laps!

159
00:15:12,790 --> 00:15:14,950
It's impossible.

160
00:15:14,950 --> 00:15:18,080
I gave up in four.

161
00:15:19,630 --> 00:15:21,160
No!

162
00:15:21,160 --> 00:15:26,800
Koyuki-kun! You must do your best,
or your dreams will never come true!

163
00:15:26,800 --> 00:15:28,800
I know.

164
00:15:28,800 --> 00:15:30,970
Just like when I made it
on the Olympic team...

165
00:15:30,970 --> 00:15:32,940
when I declared my love
to that pretty bar hostess...

166
00:15:32,940 --> 00:15:36,140
I put my mind to it!

167
00:15:36,140 --> 00:15:41,010
And...your dream came true?

168
00:15:41,010 --> 00:15:43,680
Well...The past is the past
and the present is the present.

169
00:15:43,680 --> 00:15:44,580
Huh?

170
00:15:44,580 --> 00:15:48,920
My dream came true splendidly.

171
00:15:48,920 --> 00:15:50,620
I'm...going home.

172
00:16:01,600 --> 00:16:03,590
So warm!

173
00:16:05,610 --> 00:16:10,110
Cripes! Ryusuke is such a perfectionist!

174
00:16:10,110 --> 00:16:13,740
He's gonna die all alone
when he's old and gray.

175
00:16:15,550 --> 00:16:16,480
Huh?

176
00:16:20,790 --> 00:16:22,480
The hospital...

177
00:16:28,290 --> 00:16:29,960
Hey!

178
00:16:29,960 --> 00:16:32,300
He can't handle an all-nighter.

179
00:16:32,300 --> 00:16:33,800
You'll die, for real!

180
00:16:33,800 --> 00:16:34,630
No...

181
00:16:34,630 --> 00:16:38,240
It's an important time right now.

182
00:16:38,240 --> 00:16:41,240
I can't let the band down.

183
00:16:41,240 --> 00:16:42,500
-Hmm...
-Hmm...

184
00:16:59,590 --> 00:17:01,650
All right, once more.

185
00:17:10,940 --> 00:17:14,440
Hey! What're you doing, Koyuki?

186
00:17:14,440 --> 00:17:18,110
There's been no improvement 'cuz of you!

187
00:17:18,110 --> 00:17:19,950
I-I'm sorry.

188
00:17:19,950 --> 00:17:21,550
Hey, hey!

189
00:17:21,550 --> 00:17:24,620
Look, let's take a break.

190
00:17:24,620 --> 00:17:28,380
Uh-uh...Saku, take it from the top.

191
00:17:32,790 --> 00:17:34,490
One, two!

192
00:17:47,240 --> 00:17:49,470
Where is this?

193
00:18:08,590 --> 00:18:10,620
Where...

194
00:19:00,410 --> 00:19:03,420
Oh. Made a big mess.

195
00:19:03,420 --> 00:19:04,710
Too sad.

196
00:19:06,590 --> 00:19:08,020
I'll help.

197
00:19:10,420 --> 00:19:14,090
I'm cleaning up the mess
your concert had made.

198
00:20:19,260 --> 00:20:25,200
When I woke up, my fever, which had
been as high as 103, had gone down.

199
00:20:34,770 --> 00:20:41,840
And Beck's first album was completed
around the middle of winter break.

200
00:20:59,230 --> 00:21:07,570
Uh! Typhoon! Typhoon 24! 24-7, non-stop!

201
00:21:07,570 --> 00:21:12,750
We're gonna rush at you!
Gonna send you flyin'!

202
00:21:12,750 --> 00:21:14,580
Lift up your heavy ass, now

203
00:21:14,580 --> 00:21:16,750
If you take off that stiff head

204
00:21:16,750 --> 00:21:18,980
You'll feel totally loose...

205
00:21:24,090 --> 00:21:25,760
Isn't it great?

206
00:21:25,760 --> 00:21:26,820
Yeah.

207
00:21:49,620 --> 00:21:52,120
And I thought...

208
00:21:52,120 --> 00:21:55,110
What will I be doing with my life?

209
00:21:57,120 --> 00:21:58,460
Koyuki?

210
00:21:58,460 --> 00:22:00,290
Something up?

211
00:22:00,290 --> 00:22:02,800
Nah...Nothing.

212
00:22:02,800 --> 00:22:05,800
But Saku, have you been studying?

213
00:22:05,800 --> 00:22:07,200
Not at all.

214
00:22:26,820 --> 00:22:29,490
You really haven't been studying?

215
00:22:29,490 --> 00:22:32,950
Yup...I really, really
haven't been studying.

216
00:22:36,600 --> 00:22:40,530
Everything began with this one CD.

217
00:22:50,410 --> 00:22:52,510
Another minute

218
00:22:52,510 --> 00:22:55,200
Feelin' so fine

219
00:22:57,510 --> 00:22:59,750
You turn the freeze

220
00:22:59,750 --> 00:23:02,480
into warm light

221
00:23:04,590 --> 00:23:08,060
Had a premonition

222
00:23:08,060 --> 00:23:10,730
I've been waitin' ever since

223
00:23:10,730 --> 00:23:14,230
My world comin' down

224
00:23:14,230 --> 00:23:17,030
It's got me spinnin' 'round

225
00:23:18,800 --> 00:23:24,970
If you really wanna fly

226
00:23:24,970 --> 00:23:27,740
you gotta let go

227
00:23:39,990 --> 00:23:42,320
Simply the most

228
00:23:42,320 --> 00:23:44,360
big sensation

229
00:23:44,360 --> 00:23:47,160
(once you're here you won't go back)

230
00:23:47,160 --> 00:23:49,430
She's really pretty

231
00:23:49,430 --> 00:23:51,430
One-eyed vision

232
00:23:51,430 --> 00:23:54,270
(lose the fear it don't come back)

233
00:23:54,270 --> 00:23:57,770
Little sister showed me

234
00:23:57,770 --> 00:24:00,440
Really took me for a ride

235
00:24:00,440 --> 00:24:02,110
My world comin' down

236
00:24:02,110 --> 00:24:05,450
(once you're here you won't go back)

237
00:24:05,450 --> 00:24:09,470
(lose the fear it don't come back)

238
00:24:13,760 --> 00:24:16,930
It's almost over!
Let's run towards the sun!

239
00:24:16,930 --> 00:24:18,430
It's blinding!

240
00:24:18,430 --> 00:24:20,190
I wanna be Alain Delon!
